{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_5rerw7kn2vgbvvzi2dvtx5odmlfaa36x274y5bllblyfpva3ka3q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01YA2EKtg82hqQhjywuNU5o6","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-AesDK8/translated_rust/ERRORS.md","content":"# ERRORS.md — Phase A: ERROR-SURFACE TABLE\n\nDerived **mechanically** from `c_src/src/lib.c` by grepping every\n`cp_error_reason = ...` assignment, every `goto cp_err` / `return 0` /\n`return NULL`, and every `assert(...)`. One row per distinct rejection site.\n\nThe C library is built **without `-DNDEBUG`** (no `CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE`), so\n`assert()` is live: a failed assertion calls `__assert_fail` → `abort()` →\nprocess dies with **SIGABRT (signal 6)**. The Rust translation mirrors that\nwith `cp_assert!` → `std::process::abort()`. Rows whose expected result is\n`SIGABRT` are therefore tested by spawning the `diff_harness` binary as a\nsubprocess and comparing the wait status of the C run and the Rust run.\n\nOnly two functions have external linkage: `cp_inflate` and `convert_pix`\n(see `SYMBOLS.md`). `convert_pix` has **no** error checks and returns `void`,\nso every row below is reached through `cp_inflate`.\n\nLegend for \"expected C result\":\n* `ret 0 + reason` — `cp_inflate` returns `0` **and** the global\n  `cp_error_reason` points at the quoted string.\n* `SIGABRT` — process aborts (assertion failure).\n* `SIGSEGV` — process dies from an invalid memory access.\n\n## Explicit rejections (`cp_error_reason` + `return 0`)\n\n| # | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result |\n|---|----------|----------------------------------------------|-------------------|\n| E1 | `cp_stored` (lib.c:170) | btype==0 stored block whose `LEN != (uint16_t)~NLEN` | `ret 0` + `\"Failed to find LEN and NLEN as complements within stored (uncompressed) stream.\"` |\n| E2 | `cp_stored` (lib.c:179) | btype==0 stored block where `!(s->bits_left/8 <= (int)LEN)`, i.e. more input bits remain than `LEN` bytes (e.g. a correct stored block followed by *any* extra input byte) | `ret 0` + `\"Stored block extends beyond end of input stream.\"` |\n| E3 | `cp_block` (lib.c:254) | literal symbol (<256) decoded while `!(s->out + 1 <= s->out_end)` — output buffer full / `out_bytes` too small / `out_bytes <= 0` | `ret 0` + `\"Attempted to overwrite out buffer while outputting a symbol.\"` |\n| E4 | `cp_block` (lib.c:273) | length/distance pair whose `s->out - backwards_distance < s->begin` — back-reference points before the start of the output buffer | `ret 0` + `\"Attempted to write before out buffer (invalid backwards distance).\"` |\n| E5 | `cp_block` (lib.c:282) | length/distance pair whose `s->out + length > s->out_end` — copy would run past the output buffer | `ret 0` + `\"Attempted to overwrite out buffer while outputting a string.\"` |\n| E6 | `cp_inflate` (lib.c:356) | block header `BTYPE == 3` (reserved) | `ret 0` + `\"Detected unknown block type within input stream.\"` |\n\n## Assertion rejections (`assert()` → `SIGABRT`)\n\n| # | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result |\n|---|----------|----------------------------------------------|-------------------|\n| A1 | `cp_read_bits` (lib.c:119) `assert(s->bits_left > 0)` | `in_bytes == 0` → `bits_left == 0` before the very first `cp_read_bits(s,1)` | `SIGABRT` |\n| A2 | `cp_read_bits` (lib.c:119) `assert(s->bits_left > 0)` | `in_bytes < 0` → `bits_left = in_bytes*8 <= 0` | `SIGABRT` |\n| A3 | `cp_read_bits` (lib.c:119) `assert(s->bits_left > 0)` | input exhausted mid-stream: all bits consumed and another `cp_read_bits` is issued (e.g. 1-byte input `0x00` → btype 0 → the 16-bit `LEN` read finds `bits_left == 0`) | `SIGABRT` |\n| A4 | `cp_read_bits` (lib.c:121) `assert(!cp_would_overflow(s, n))` | `(bits_left + count) - n < 0`: a read is issued that needs more bits than the stream can still supply while `bits_left` is still `> 0` (e.g. 2-byte truncated btype-0 header, `LEN` read of 16 bits with only 5 bits left) | `SIGABRT` |\n| A5 | `cp_consume_bits` (lib.c:109) `assert(s->count >= n)` | truncated Huffman stream: `cp_decode` peaks, the buffer holds fewer bits than the matched code length (`key & 0xF`), so the consume asserts | `SIGABRT` |\n| A6 | `cp_ptr` (lib.c:89) `assert(!(s->bits_left & 7))` | btype==0 reached with `bits_left` not a multiple of 8 after `LEN`/`NLEN` — i.e. a stored block in a stream whose remaining bit count is not byte-aligned | `SIGABRT` |\n| A7 | `cp_decode` (lib.c:211) `assert((search >> len) == (key >> len))` | the Huffman table does not contain a prefix matching the next bits. Deterministically reachable with a btype==2 block whose 4+`HCLEN` code-length code lengths are **all zero** → `s->nlen == 0` → `hi == 0` → `lo == 0` → `key = tree[-1]` (reads `s->dst[31]`, zero after `calloc`) → `len = 32-0 = 32` → `search>>32 == search != 0 == key>>32` | `SIGABRT` |\n| A8 | `cp_build` (lib.c:148) `assert(len < 16)` | a code length `>= 16` is fed to `cp_build`. **Unreachable via the exported API**: `cp_fixed_table` holds only {5,7,8,9}; `cp_dynamic`'s `lenlens[]` come from `cp_read_bits(s,3)` ∈ [0,7]; `lens[]` come from `cp_decode` over a 19-symbol tree so ∈ [0,18] with 16/17/18 handled by the repeat cases → ∈ [0,15]. Documented, not testable. | *unreachable* |\n| A9 | `cp_peak_bits` (lib.c:98) `assert(s->word_index <= s->word_count)` | **Unreachable**: guarded by the enclosing `if (s->word_index < s->word_count)`, so after the post-increment `word_index <= word_count` always holds. | *unreachable* |\n| A10 | `cp_read_bits` (lib.c:117/118) `assert(n <= 32)`, `assert(n >= 0)` | **Unreachable**: every call site passes a literal (1,2,3,4,5,16), `s->count & 7` ∈ [0,7], `cp_len_extra_bits[0..30]` ∈ [0,5] or `cp_dist_extra_bits[0..31]` ∈ [0,13]. Documented, not testable. | *unreachable* |\n| A11 | `cp_read_bits` (lib.c:120) `assert(s->count <= 64)` | **Unreachable**: `cp_peak_bits` only tops `count` up when `count < n <= 32`, adding at most 32 (or `bits_left`), and `count` is only ever decremented elsewhere; it can never exceed 64 at the head of `cp_read_bits`. Documented, not testable. | *unreachable* |\n\n## Non-assert rejections in unreachable (dead) code\n\n`cp_unfilter`, `cp_chunk` and `cp_find` are `static` and have **no caller** in\nthe translation unit (see `SYMBOLS.md`), so these rows cannot be observed\nthrough the `.so` ABI. Listed for completeness of the mechanical grep.\n\n| # | function | trigger | expected C result |\n|---|----------|---------|-------------------|\n| E12 | `cp_unfilter` (lib.c:434) | row-0 filter byte not in {0,1,2,3,4} | `return 0` — *unreachable* |\n| E13 | `cp_unfilter` (lib.c:468) | row-`y>0` filter byte not in {0,1,2,3,4} | `return 0` — *unreachable* |\n| E14 | `cp_chunk` (lib.c:397) / `cp_find` (lib.c:409) | chunk tag mismatch, `len < minlen`, or chunk running past `png->end` | `return NULL` — *unreachable* |\n\n## Generic FFI-boundary boundary cases (tested even though not in the grep)\n\n| # | entry point | trigger | expected C result |\n|---|-------------|---------|-------------------|\n| G1 | `cp_inflate` | `in == NULL`, `in_bytes == 0` | `SIGABRT` (A1 fires before the NULL is dereferenced) |\n| G2 | `cp_inflate` | `in == NULL`, `in_bytes > 0` | `SIGSEGV` (reads `s->words[0]` at address 0) |\n| G3 | `cp_inflate` | `out == NULL`, `out_bytes == 0`, valid non-empty stream | `ret 0` + E3 string (`out+1 <= out_end` is false) |\n| G4 | `cp_inflate` | `out_bytes == 0` (valid pointer), stream that emits ≥1 literal | `ret 0` + E3 string |\n| G5 | `cp_inflate` | `out_bytes < 0` | `ret 0` + E3 string (`out_end < out`) |\n| G6 | `cp_inflate` | `out_bytes` exactly one byte short of the true output size | `ret 0` + E3 or E5 string |\n| G7 | `cp_inflate` | `out_bytes == INT_MAX` with a valid stream | `ret 1`, correct bytes |\n| G8 | `cp_inflate` | `in_bytes == 1` for each of the 4 BTYPE values (BTYPE is a 2-bit field read from the stream — all 4 values 0..3 are exercised, including the out-of-range/reserved 3) | see A3/A4/A5/E6 |\n| G9 | `cp_inflate` | `in_bytes` larger than the real stream (trailing garbage) | E2 for stored; for btype 1/2 the extra bytes are simply never read → `ret 1` |\n| G10 | `cp_inflate` | `in_bytes` smaller than the real stream (truncation at every prefix length) | `ret 0` (E3/E4/E5) or `SIGABRT` (A3/A4/A5/A7) — must match C exactly |\n| G11 | `convert_pix` | `bpp` outside the `switch`: 0, 5, -1, `INT_MIN`, `INT_MAX` (a C `int`/enum-like selector accepts any value) | no write to `dst`; `src` still advanced by `1 + w*bpp` per row; returns void |\n| G12 | `convert_pix` | `w == 0`, `h == 0`, `w < 0`, `h < 0` | no-op (loop conditions false) |\n| G13 | `convert_pix` | `src == NULL` / `dst == NULL` with `w == 0` or `h == 0` | no-op, no dereference |\n\n## Verification checklist (Phase C)\n\n| row | test | status |\n|-----|------|--------|\n| E1  | `tests/errors.rs::e1_stored_len_nlen_mismatch`            | [x] |\n| E2  | `tests/errors.rs::e2_stored_block_extends_beyond`         | [x] |\n| E3  | `tests/errors.rs::e3_out_overflow_symbol`                 | [x] |\n| E4  | `tests/errors.rs::e4_invalid_backwards_distance`          | [x] |\n| E5  | `tests/errors.rs::e5_out_overflow_string`                 | [x] |\n| E6  | `tests/errors.rs::e6_unknown_block_type`                  | [x] |\n| A1  | `tests/aborts.rs::a1_zero_in_bytes`                       | [x] |\n| A2  | `tests/aborts.rs::a2_negative_in_bytes`                   | [x] |\n| A3  | `tests/aborts.rs::a3_input_exhausted`                     | [x] |\n| A4  | `tests/aborts.rs::a4_would_overflow`                      | [x] |\n| A5  | `tests/aborts.rs::a5_consume_bits_underflow`              | [x] |\n| A6  | `tests/aborts.rs::a6_cp_ptr_misaligned`                   | [x] |\n| A7  | `tests/aborts.rs::a7_decode_no_prefix`                    | [x] |\n| A8  | unreachable —