{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_47fn2yz453ih5hoaatlzllp2f7x3uyixux2v5rdod4yh4ybfxyqq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01D77zHauJ1kzRJDsEYQ7wTa","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-AesDK8/translated_rust/CONFIGS.md","content":"# CONFIGS.md — Phase A: CONFIGURATION-SURFACE TABLE (valid inputs)\n\nDerived **mechanically** from `c_src/src/lib.c`: every `if` / `switch` / loop\ncondition the code branches on for *valid* input, plus every distinct input\n*shape* the code special-cases.\n\n## Public entry points (the complete set — see `SYMBOLS.md`)\n\n| kind | symbol | signature |\n|---|---|---|\n| function | `convert_pix` | `void convert_pix(int bpp, int w, int h, uint8_t *src, cp_pixel_t *dst)` |\n| function | `cp_inflate`  | `int cp_inflate(void *in, int in_bytes, void *out, int out_bytes)` |\n| data | `cp_error_reason` | `const char *` — set by `cp_inflate`'s failure paths |\n| data | `cp_fixed_table` | `uint8_t[320]` — **read by `cp_fixed`**, so mutating it changes `cp_inflate` |\n| data | `cp_permutation_order` | `uint8_t[19]` — **read by `cp_dynamic`** |\n| data | `cp_len_extra_bits` | `uint8_t[31]` — **read by `cp_block`** |\n| data | `cp_len_base` | `uint32_t[31]` — **read by `cp_block`** |\n| data | `cp_dist_extra_bits` | `uint8_t[32]` — **read by `cp_block`** |\n| data | `cp_dist_base` | `uint32_t[32]` — **read by `cp_block`** |\n\n`cp_inflate` is itself the lowest-level exported entry point; the bit reader\n(`cp_read_bits`/`cp_peak_bias`), the Huffman table builder (`cp_build`), the\nsymbol decoder (`cp_decode`) and the three block decoders (`cp_stored`,\n`cp_fixed`, `cp_dynamic` → `cp_block`) are `static` and are driven **only**\nthrough `cp_inflate`. Every row below therefore states which internal\nlow-level paths it forces, and the tests drive them by constructing raw DEFLATE\nbit streams directly (not just by calling a one-shot convenience wrapper).\n\n## Branch axes the C actually distinguishes\n\n### `cp_inflate`\n| axis | values the C branches on | source |\n|---|---|---|\n| `BTYPE` | 0 (stored), 1 (fixed Huffman), 2 (dynamic Huffman) | `switch (btype)` lib.c:333 |\n| `BFINAL` | 0 → loop again, 1 → stop | `do {...} while (!bfinal)` lib.c:365 |\n| input pointer alignment | `first_bytes = ((in+3)&~3) - in` ∈ {0,1,2,3} — changes `s->words`, `s->word_count`, the pre-seeded `s->bits`, and `s->count` | lib.c:314-324 |\n| `in_bytes - first_bytes` mod 4 | `last_bytes` ∈ {0,1,2,3} — `final_word_available` 0 vs 1, which selects the `else if` arm of `cp_peak_bits` | lib.c:317-323 |\n| `word_count` | 0 (no full words → `final_word` arm only) vs ≥1 | `if (s->word_index < s->word_count)` lib.c:94 |\n| `out_bytes` | exact vs. larger than the true output | `s->out_end` checks lib.c:254, 282 |\n\n### `cp_stored` (BTYPE 0)\n| axis | values | source |\n|---|---|---|\n| `s->count & 7` | 0 (already byte aligned) vs 1..7 (pad bits read) | lib.c:166 |\n| `LEN` | 0 (empty stored block), 1, 2, 3, 4, 5.., 65535 | `memcpy(s->out, p, LEN)` lib.c:187 |\n| `bits_left/8 <= LEN` | equal (only accepted case) vs greater (E2) | lib.c:179 |\n\n### `cp_build` (Huffman table construction)\n| axis | values | source |\n|---|---|---|\n| `s` | non-NULL → the 512-entry `lookup` table is zeroed and filled; NULL → skipped | `if (s)` lib.c:143, 152 |\n| code length | 0 (skipped), 1..9 (also enters the `lookup` loop), 10..15 (`tree` only) | `if (len != 0)`, `if (s && len <= 9)` lib.c:147, 152 |\n| `sym_count` | 288 (`lit`, fixed), 32 (`dst`, fixed), 19 (`len`), `nlit` ∈ [257,288], `ndst` ∈ [1,32] | lib.c:194-195, 223, 245-246 |\n\n### `cp_decode`\n| axis | values | source |\n|---|---|---|\n| `hi` | 0 (empty tree → `tree[-1]`, see ERRORS A7) vs ≥1 | `while (lo < hi)` lib.c:202 |\n| `key & 0xF` | 1..15 (code length actually consumed) | lib.c:212 |\n\n### `cp_dynamic` (BTYPE 2)\n| axis | values | source |\n|---|---|---|\n| `HLIT`  | `nlit = 257 + read(5)` ∈ [257, 288] | lib.c:218 |\n| `HDIST` | `ndst = 1 + read(5)`   ∈ [1, 32]   | lib.c:219 |\n| `HCLEN` | `nlen = 4 + read(4)`   ∈ [4, 19]   | lib.c:220 |\n| code-length symbol | 0..15 (literal length), 16 (copy previous 3..6), 17 (zero run 3..10), 18 (zero run 11..138) | `switch (sym)` lib.c:227 |\n\n### `cp_block`\n| axis | values | source |\n|---|---|---|\n| symbol class | `< 256` literal, `== 256` end-of-block, `> 256` length/distance | lib.c:252, 264, 301 |\n| length symbol | 257..285 → `cp_len_extra_bits[0..28]` ∈ {0..5}, `cp_len_base[0..28]` ∈ {3..258}; 286/287 → base 0 | lib.c:266-267 |\n| distance symbol | 0..29 → `cp_dist_extra_bits` ∈ {0..13}, `cp_dist_base` ∈ {1..24577}; 30/31 → base 0 | lib.c:268-271 |\n| `backwards_distance` | **1 → `memset` fast path**; anything else → byte-by-byte forward copy (so overlapping copies with distance < length must replicate byte-wise) | `switch (backwards_distance)` lib.c:293 |\n\n### `convert_pix`\n| axis | values | source |\n|---|---|---|\n| `bpp` | 1 (gray), 2 (gray+alpha), 3 (rgb), 4 (rgba), anything else (no `dst` write but `src` still advances) | `switch (bpp)` lib.c:477 |\n| `w`   | 0, 1, 2, many | `for (x = 0; x < w; ...)` lib.c:476 |\n| `h`   | 0, 1, 2, many | `for (y = 0; y < h; ...)` lib.c:474 |\n\n## Rows — one per meaningful COMBINATION (pruned cross-product)\n\n`R` = randomized with a fixed seed, many inputs per row.\n\"alignment sweep\" = the same payload placed at input-buffer offsets 0,1,2,3 so\n`first_bytes` takes all 4 values; \"tail sweep\" = payload lengths chosen so\n`last_bytes` takes all 4 values.\n\n### `convert_pix`\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| C1 | `convert_pix` | `bpp=1`, `w×h` = (1,1),(2,1),(1,2),(3,3),(17,5),(64,64) + R random `w,h` ∈[0,40]; random `src` | [x] |\n| C2 | `convert_pix` | `bpp=2`, same shape sweep + R | [x] |\n| C3 | `convert_pix` 