# | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| F1 | `cp_inflate` | hand-built fixed block: end-of-block only (empty output), `out_bytes` 0 and >0 | [x] |\n| F2 | `cp_inflate` | hand-built fixed block: literals only, using symbols from **both** fixed-table length classes (0..143 → 8 bits, 144..255 → 9 bits) | [x] |\n| F3 | `cp_inflate` | hand-built fixed block: every length symbol 257..285 (all `cp_len_extra_bits` values 0..5, all `cp_len_base` values 3..258) at distance 1 → **`memset` path** | [x] |\n| F4 | `cp_inflate` | hand-built fixed block: every length symbol 257..285 at distance 2 → **byte-copy path**, overlapping (length > distance) | [x] |\n| F5 | `cp_inflate` | hand-built fixed block: every distance symbol 0..29 (all `cp_dist_extra_bits` 0..13, all `cp_dist_base` 1..24577) with enough preceding output | [x] |\n| F6 | `cp_inflate` | hand-built fixed block: length symbols 286 and 287 (`cp_len_base` == 0 → zero-length copy) | [x] |\n| F7 | `cp_inflate` | hand-built fixed block: distance symbols 30 and 31 (`cp_dist_base` == 0 → distance 0, `out - 0 >= begin` passes, `memset`/copy with distance 0) | [x] |\n| F8 | `cp_inflate` | `flate2` raw-deflate at `Compression::fast()` of R random payloads (mixed literals + matches) — real-encoder streams | [x] |\n| F9 | `cp_inflate` | F2/F3/F8 payloads × **alignment sweep** × **tail sweep** | [x] |\n| F10 | `cp_inflate` | multi-block: two or more fixed blocks with `BFINAL=0` then a final one — exercises the `while (!bfinal)` loop and table rebuild | [x] |\n\n### `cp_inflate` — BTYPE 2 (dynamic Huffman) — drives `cp_dynamic`, `cp_build` ×3, `cp_decode` ×2\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| D1 | `cp_inflate` | hand-built dynamic block, minimal: `HLIT=257`, `HDIST=1`, `HCLEN=4`, single literal + EOB | [x] |\n| D2 | `cp_inflate` | hand-built dynamic block with `HCLEN=19` (all 19 `cp_permutation_order` slots read) | [x] |\n| D3 | `cp_inflate` | hand-built dynamic block with `HLIT=288`, `HDIST=32` (maxima) | [x] |\n| D4 | `cp_inflate` | hand-built dynamic block using code-length symbol **16** (copy-previous, repeat 3..6) | [x] |\n| D5 | `cp_inflate` | hand-built dynamic block using code-length symbol **17** (zero run 3..10) | [x] |\n| D6 | `cp_inflate` | hand-built dynamic block using code-length symbol **18** (zero run 11..138) | [x] |\n| D7 | `cp_inflate` | hand-built dynamic block whose literal code lengths reach 10..15 (so `cp_build`'s `len <= 9` lookup branch is *not* taken for those symbols) | [x] |\n| D8 | `cp_inflate` | `flate2` raw-deflate at `Compression::best()` / `default()` of R random and structured payloads (real encoder emits dynamic blocks) | [x] |\n| D9 | `cp_inflate` | D8 payloads × **alignment sweep** × **tail sweep** | [x] |\n| D10 | `cp_inflate` | payload shapes that force distance-1 runs (`memset` path) inside a dynamic block: long runs of a single byte | [x] |\n| D11 | `cp_inflate` | payload shapes with long-range matches (distance up to 24576) inside a dynamic block: 32 KiB of repeating structured data | [x] |\n| D12 | `cp_inflate` | multi-block: dynamic → dynamic → final; and mixed stored → fixed → dynamic → final in one stream | [x] |\n| D13 | `cp_inflate` | `flate2` output of the *empty* input (produces a block that decodes to 0 bytes) | [x] |\n\n### Cross-cutting\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| X1 | `cp_error_reason`, `cp_fixed_table`, `cp_permutation_order`, `cp_len_extra_bits`, `cp_len_base`, `cp_dist_extra_bits`, `cp_dist_base` | byte-for-byte comparison of every exported data object between the two `.so`s (and `cp_error_reason == NULL` before any call) | [x] |\n| X2 | `cp_inflate` | after a **successful** call, `cp_error_reason` is unchanged in both (the C never clears it) | [x] |\n| X3 | `cp_inflate` | the whole 128 KiB output arena (not just `out_bytes`) is compared, so any over-write past `out_bytes` must match too | [x] |\n| X4 | `cp_inflate` | the input arena is compared after the call: neither implementation may modify the input | [x] |\n| X5 | `cp_inflate` | R fuzz: 20 000 short pseudo-random byte strings (2..24 bytes) at all 4 alignments, comparing return value, `cp_error_reason` string and the whole output arena; runs in a subprocess pair so `SIGABRT`/`SIGSEGV` outcomes are compared too | [x] |\n| X6 | `cp_inflate` | R fuzz: bit-flipped mutations of *valid* streams (1–3 flipped bits) — same comparison as X5 | [x] |\n\n## Notes on inputs deliberately excluded\n\nTwo input classes make the **C** program execute constructs whose behaviour is\nnot determined by the C abstract machine *and* not determined by the generated\ncode either, so no byte-identical Rust translation is definable:\n\n1. **`cp_dynamic` code-length repeat overrun.** `uint8_t lens[288+32]` is a\n   stack array; a repeat code at `n` close to `nlit+ndst` writes up to\n   `lens[nlit+ndst+136]`, i.e. up to 137 bytes past the array, corrupting the\n   C stack frame (`nlit`, `ndst`, `n`, `s`, the return address …). The Rust\n   uses a padded buffer. Real DEFLATE encoders never emit this.\n2. **`cp_dynamic` code-length symbol 16 at `n == 0`.** C reads `lens[-1]`,\n   which is uninitialised stack memory.\n\nThe fuzz rows X5/X6 keep inputs short (≤ 24 bytes) and mutate only 1–3 bits of\nvalid streams, which cannot reach case 1 (it needs a well-formed 19-symbol\ncode-length tree plus ~300 emitted lengths), and case 2 is filtered by the\nharness (it reports \"skipped\" rather than a mismatch) — see\n`tests/common/mod.rs::UB_SKIP`.\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5378,"cache_read_input_tokens":82564,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_